{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "025A", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-structure-etale-map}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d57fba65c931e0f492491364ebabfa2e500c05823bb0c7ca930b067223886f4e", "source_text": "The structure theorem", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cc81d5a43aa3ac34f26f00b088eb9f1bdada58ba6e3bf8c1c472b3b1fbcb885f", "unit_id": "tag:025A:title"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "025A", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0005": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0006": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0007": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0008": "\\'e", "ITEMCLOSE_0001": "]", "ITEMCLOSE_0002": "]", "ITEMOPEN_0001": "\\item[", "ITEMOPEN_0002": "\\item[", "MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$f, g \\in R[t]$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f' = \\text{d}f/\\text{d}t$", "MATH_0005": "$R[t]_g/(f)$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nR \\longrightarrow R[t]_g/(f) = R[t, 1/g]/(f)\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$$\nR \\longrightarrow R[t]_{f'}/(f) = R[t, 1/f']/(f)\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-definition-standard-etale}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:05f74048b613c8ebebd12825fb2aebdf5b2b6997991c3548ff25af2f2ab70c9b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eedf9a9601414e271d434cb8246e8fbea90e5a77a1fef4c525548ad0d998a216", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe present a theorem which describes the local structure of <ACCENT_0001>tale\nand unramified morphisms. Besides its obvious independent importance,\nthis theorem also allows us to make the transition to another\ndefinition of <ACCENT_0002>tale morphisms that captures the geometric intuition better\nthan the one we've used so far.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nTo state it we need the notion of a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>standard <ACCENT_0003>tale ring map<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, see\nAlgebra, Definition <REF_0001>.\nNamely, suppose that <MATH_0001> is a ring and <MATH_0002> are polynomials\nsuch that\n<STRUCT_0004>\n<ITEMOPEN_0001>(a)<ITEMCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0003> is a monic polynomial, and\n<ITEMOPEN_0002>(b)<ITEMCLOSE_0002> <MATH_0004> is invertible in the localization\n<MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nThen the map\n<MATH_0006>\nis a standard <ACCENT_0004>tale algebra, and any standard <ACCENT_0005>tale algebra is isomorphic\nto one of these. It is a pleasant exercise to prove that such a ring map\nis flat, and unramified and hence <ACCENT_0006>tale (as expected of course).\nA special case of a standard <ACCENT_0007>tale ring map is any ring map\n<MATH_0007>\nwith <MATH_0008> a monic polynomial, and any standard <ACCENT_0008>tale algebra is (isomorphic to)\na principal localization of one of these.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b733cca25ba736c5c3fac92bafe0427c2168000468ccc67d196034eac819a16d", "unit_id": "tag:025A:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "025A", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$f, g \\in A[t]$", "MATH_0003": "$B' = A[t]_g/(f)$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$B'$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-structure-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1935783b9b0adcc653e5b07720684b60b6d80d2cbf52c766a9ca726b97fa87a9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5bcab4cfbf2ce2b85af1c1097cc4794aef48a239490a9fca2dc0cf1833279218", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an <ACCENT_0001>tale homomorphism of local rings.\nThen there exist <MATH_0002> such that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is standard <ACCENT_0002>tale -- see (a) and (b) above, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0004> is isomorphic to a localization of <MATH_0005> at a prime.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:311c85a7961cb39bb1c778fded93dc4b0d048617bbb60e7af95cee372f842c74", "unit_id": "tag:025B:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "025A", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$B = B'_{\\mathfrak q}$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$B'$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$A$", "MATH_0006": "$A \\to B'$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0008": "$B'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-etale-Noetherian}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-proposition-etale-locally-standard}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9cf57c9a35704d606196d80da14fe16d778696330b61dc317fccf94130a44978", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2db9e3bd9f13bf59ae6d75b969b1bd504bb95119b0dc47706747de2a7d720b87", "source_text": "Write <MATH_0001> for some finite type <MATH_0002>-algebra <MATH_0003>\n(we can do this because <MATH_0004> is essentially of finite type over <MATH_0005>).\nBy Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe see that <MATH_0006> is <ACCENT_0001>tale at <MATH_0007>.\nHence we may apply\nAlgebra, Proposition <REF_0002>\nto see that a principal localization of <MATH_0008> is standard <ACCENT_0002>tale.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cf13c429453cc6a92c644242fe0fb70549d860a0de19fa581b57319feabb8acc", "unit_id": "tag:025B:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "025A", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fef742a8e9be4a2562a5fbd11df685dd022326ae610f4dff03716410d60b5760", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the version for unramified homomorphisms of local rings.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9b0aed1e566210d3bcaa22396bd94bc6a016ae0757828dbd01964f8e040d39c6", "unit_id": "tag:025A:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "025A", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$f, g \\in A[t]$", "MATH_0003": "$B' = A[t]_g/(f)$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$B'$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-structure-unramified}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1935783b9b0adcc653e5b07720684b60b6d80d2cbf52c766a9ca726b97fa87a9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:17bd82e5f3c070f92e81a044f939d440b7f02d2829aa0d5d8a2430aade8bf828", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an unramified morphism of local rings.\nThen there exist <MATH_0002> such that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is standard <ACCENT_0001>tale -- see (a) and (b) above, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0004> is isomorphic to a quotient of a localization of <MATH_0005> at a prime.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:79c6d9424522b67bed77f92f77da26be3a15430ff59fd4981acc1c21dc1c1067", "unit_id": "tag:039O:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "025A", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$B = B'_{\\mathfrak q}$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$B'$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$A$", "MATH_0006": "$A \\to B'$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0008": "$B'$", "MATH_0009": "$A$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-unramified-Noetherian}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-proposition-unramified-locally-standard}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:39643b934d5b9b462fac7a330e0623e637ae1868aa4589de413a99beae5506a2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8e07bd69fb47cd42a3d68432b13ae9889ed4645f12466320a7e040567244a438", "source_text": "Write <MATH_0001> for some finite type <MATH_0002>-algebra <MATH_0003>\n(we can do this because <MATH_0004> is essentially of finite type over <MATH_0005>).\nBy Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe see that <MATH_0006> is unramified at <MATH_0007>.\nHence we may apply\nAlgebra, Proposition <REF_0002>\nto see that a principal localization of <MATH_0008> is a quotient of a\nstandard <ACCENT_0001>tale <MATH_0009>-algebra.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fbd93a879b3677ded802dca47a1c594654fa664f8799702596530119ca0310ed", "unit_id": "tag:039O:proof"}
